        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Abraham</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">placed by tradition in the early 2nd millennium BCE</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Born</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/book-of-genesis">Book of Genesis</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a> of the Chaldees, the son of Terah; some exegetes such as Nahmanides place his birth in Haran; no date is given</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Died</span><span class="info-stat-val">According to Genesis at age 175, buried in the cave of Machpelah near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebron">Hebron</a> beside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarah">Sarah</a> by his sons <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac">Isaac</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishmael">Ishmael</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Who they were</span><span class="info-stat-val">In <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judaism">Judaism</a> the ethnic ancestor and first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew">Hebrew</a> patriarch; in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> the forebear of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesus">Jesus</a> and the spiritual ancestor of all Christians; in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> a prophet in the chain from Adam to Muhammad</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">the call to leave Haran for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canaan">Canaan</a>; the covenant with God; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hagar">Hagar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ishmael">Ishmael</a>; the birth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isaac">Isaac</a>; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/binding-of-isaac">binding of Isaac</a>; the purchase of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cave-of-the-patriarchs">Cave of the Patriarchs</a></span></div>
